  "description": "This package contains ready-to-run Progress® Telerik® Reporting project templates for the .NET CLI. After installing the package with \"dotnet new install Telerik.Reporting.CLITemplates\", you can scaffold a new project from the terminal with \"dotnet new <template-short-name>\".\n\n            The package provides four templates that default to .NET 10 and can target .NET 8, .NET 9, or .NET 10:\n            - telerik-reporting-html5 — ASP.NET Core app with the HTML5 (jQuery) Report Viewer.\n            - telerik-reporting-angular — Angular app with the Native Angular Report Viewer and a companion ASP.NET Core reporting service.\n            - telerik-reporting-blazor — Blazor Web App with the Native Blazor Report Viewer.\n            - telerik-web-report-designer — ASP.NET Core app hosting the Web Report Designer.\n\n            The generated projects reference the required Telerik Reporting NuGet packages. This templates package itself does not add any runtime dependencies to your solution.\n\n            IMPORTANT: This is commercial software. To use it, you must agree to the Telerik End User License Agreement for Telerik Reporting (https://www.telerik.com/purchase/license-agreement/reporting-dlw-s).\n            If you do not have a commercial license, the usage of this product is governed by the trial license terms.\n            Telerik Reporting requires activation using a license key — this applies to both the trial and commercial versions of the product.\n\n            Telerik Reporting licenses can be obtained through the Telerik Reporting page (https://www.telerik.com/purchase/individual/reporting). For more information on licensing, configuration, and troubleshooting, refer to the product documentation's License section (https://docs.telerik.com/reporting/licensing/setting-up-your-telerik-reporting-license-key).",
  "iconFile": "images\\progress.png",
